Its status declined during the 12th century mainly due to the fact that the participants of the Crusade had returned bringing gifts such as silks and spices, which were worth more than what the Byzantine markets offered.
It was at this time that there was the transfer of the title of Fashion Capital from Constantinople to Paris.
