Subsistency agriculture is agriculture carried out for the production of food sufficient to meet only the needs of farmers and their families.
Subsistent agriculture is a simple, usually organic system that uses native guarded seeds from the ecorregion, combined with crop rotation or other relatively simple techniques to maximize production.
Historically, most farmers have been involved with subsistence agriculture, and this is still the case in most developing nations.
Subcultures bring together like-minded individuals who feel overlooked by society’s standards and allow them to develop a sense of identity.
Subcultures can be distinct due to the age, ethnicity, class, location and/or gender of the members.
The qualities that determine a subculture as distinct can be linguistic, aesthetic, religious, political, sexual, geographical or a combination of factors.
Members of a subculture often signal their affiliation through a distinct and symbolic use of style, which includes fashions, mannerisms and jargon.
