German sweets are very good and, in Bavaria, they are very whimsical and varied, similar to those of the southern neighbor, Austria.
Candies with fruits are recurrent, with baked apples in sweets all year round, and cherries and plums marking presence during the summer.
Many German bakery merchandise also has almonds, hazelnuts and other chestnuts. Famous cakes usually combine very well with a very strong cup of coffee.
If you want some small but tasty sweets, try what, depending on the region, can be called Berliner, Pfannkuchen or Krapfen.
A curry is a dish based on herbs and spices, together with meat or vegetables.
A curry can be "dry" or "wet" depending on the amount of liquid.
In regions of the interior of Northern India and Pakistan, yogurt is commonly used in curries; in southern India and other coastal regions of the subcontinent, coconut milk is commonly used.
With 17,000 islands to choose from, Indonesian cuisine is a fan that encompasses a wide variety of regional cuisines found across the country.
