In order for the feet of a knight to have support, stirrups are used, which hang on both sides of the saddle.
They provide greater stability for the knight, but can present safety problems, as the feet of the knight can get stuck in them.
If a rider is thrown from a horse, but had one of his feet clinging to the stirrup, he can be dragged if the animal ends up fleeing. To decrease this danger, several safety preventions can be taken
First, a large part of the riders wear mounting boots with heel and smooth sole, which is quite narrow.
