Snow sports, which include skiing and snowboarding, are popular sports that involve gliding over snow-covered terrain with skis or a snowboard attached to your feet.
Skiing is an important trip activity for many enthusiasts, occasionally known as "ski bums," who plan entire vacations just to ski in a specific location.
The idea of skiing is very old — cave paintings depicting skiers, dating back to 5000 B.C!
Alpine ski as a sport dates back to the 17th century at least and in the year 1861, the first recreational skiing team was opened by citizens of Norway in Australia.
Ski backpacking: activity also known as sertão skiing, walking skiing or ski-alpinism.
It's related, but usually doesn't involve tourism for alpine skiing or mountaineering, the latest feats on steep terrain and requiring much stiffer skies and boots.
