Europe is a relatively small continent but with many independent countries. Under normal circumstances, traveling through several countries would mean having to go through visa applications and passport control several times.
The Schengen zone, however, functions as a country in this respect.
If you stay in this area, it is possible to cross the border without going through passport checkpoints again.
Similarly, owning a Schengen visa, you will not need to apply for visas for each of the Schengen member countries separately, thus saving time, money and paperwork.
