Bad weather is the generic term for any dangerous climate phenomenon with the potential to cause harm, serious social disturbances, or loss of human lives.
Poor weather can occur anywhere in the world and encompasses different types, which vary according to the geographical location, topography and weather conditions.
Strong winds, hail, excessive precipitation and wildfires are forms and effects of a harsh climate, as well as storms, tornadoes, water trunks and cyclones.
Severe regional and seasonal weather phenomena include blizzards, as well as snowstorms, ice and dust.
Travelers are strongly advised to be mindful of any risk of bad weather in their region as this can affect travel plans.
