Christmas is one of the most important holidays in Christianity and is celebrated as the birthday of Jesus.
Many of the traditions of the holiday were also adopted by non-believers in Christian and non-Christian countries around the world.
There is a tradition of spending Easter night awake somewhere open to see the sunrise.
There are, of course, Christian theological explanations for this tradition, but it may be a pre-Christian ritual of spring and fertility.
The most traditional churches often hold an Easter vigil on Saturday night during the Easter weekend. Congregations often break the celebration at midnight to celebrate Christ’s resurrection.
