As the areas are sparely inhabited, and consequently light pollution is not a problem, you will also be able to appreciate the stars.
In Japan, labor cultural relations are more based on hierarchy and formality than Westerners are used to seeing.
Suits are the standard suit in business, and co-workers call each other by their surnames or positions.
Harmony in the workplace is crucial, emphasizing group effort rather than praising individual achievements.
Workers usually need the approval of their superiors for all the decisions they make, and they are expected to obey the instructions of their superiors without question.
